summary:
  Unticking the one device that played leaves the widget casting to one that refused.

history:
  A television and a Ruark R5se were ticked; the television played, the
  Ruark refused. Unticking the television left nobody playing and nobody
  being asked, but the flag was only lowered when the last TICK went, and
  the Ruark's was still up: "Casting to Ruark R5se" came back over a
  silent room (2026-11-11). The flag follows the record of who carries the
  stream. No sound is started here for it: the listener unticked a device,
  and Play is theirs to press.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
              if (!CastLogic.carried(_castSession)) _castEnd();   // a refused device stays ticked: the last that played can leave with ticks up

replace:
              if (targets.length === 0) _castEnd();   // a refused device stays ticked: the last that played can leave with ticks up

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_device_that_refused_the_stream_is_not_cast_to.
  Line-neutral.
